.TH ADA 1 "August 2026" "v1.8.1" "Ada Manual"
.SH NAME
Ada \- Desktop Virtual Assistant.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ada
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Ada
is a desktop virtual assistant with a graphical user interface. It allows interaction with artificial intelligence models via OpenRouter and also offers a completely local, offline mode using a quantized GGUF model.
.PP
The application saves its configuration and conversation memory on the user's computer. When run for the first time, it prompts for initial setup to enter credentials and select the artificial intelligence model.
.SH FEATURES
.TP
.B Artificial intelligence engine
Low-latency connection with available models through OpenRouter.
.TP
.B Persistent memory
Saves conversation history locally in a cyclic buffer named
.I memories.json .
.TP
.B Text-to-speech
Responds via voice in Spanish. On Windows it uses SAPI with the Microsoft Sabina voice; on Linux it uses PicoTTS.
.TP
.B Speech-to-text
Uses Vosk to transcribe voice prompts. Press Shift+F1 inside the application to activate this feature and press Enter to send the transcribed text.
.TP
.B System control
Can shut down or restart the computer, open applications and websites, execute system commands, and create reminders for today or tomorrow.
.TP
.B Interactive gestures
Ada's expression changes depending on the topic of the conversation.
.TP
.B Offline mode
Allows the use of a local model without an Internet connection. It requires at least 8 GB of RAM; 16 GB is recommended to use it while running multiple applications.
.SH INITIAL CONFIGURATION
The online mode requires an OpenRouter API key. Register or log in to OpenRouter, create an API key using the "New Key" option, and keep it in a safe place.
.PP
On the first launch, enter the API key when prompted by the application and choose the artificial intelligence model you wish to use.
.SH USAGE
To launch Ada from a terminal, execute:
.PP
.EX
ada
.EE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/ada/
Directory that stores Ada's configuration and the API key.
.TP
.I ~/.config/ada/AdaOffline.Q4_K_M.gguf
Default location of the offline language model, if downloaded.
